WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.458 --> 00:00:03.994
&gt;&gt; With a tattoo of his mother.

00:00:04.127 --> 00:00:04.728
Sara sidner, thank you so much

00:00:04.861 --> 00:00:05.696
for being with us.

00:00:05.829 --> 00:00:07.831
Keep us posted.

00:00:07.965 --> 00:00:13.470
&gt;&gt;&gt; Now Antonio Romanucci.

00:00:13.537 --> 00:00:15.939
He is one of the attorneys

00:00:16.073 --> 00:00:17.474
representing Tyre Nichols's

00:00:17.474 --> 00:00:18.508
family.
Thank you so much for being with

00:00:18.642 --> 00:00:19.710
us.
I'm sorry it is under these

00:00:19.843 --> 00:00:20.310
circumstances.

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:21.712
How is Mr. Nichols' family doing

00:00:21.845 --> 00:00:24.314
now that the officers have been

00:00:24.448 --> 00:00:24.815
indicted?

00:00:24.815 --> 00:00:26.917
&gt;&gt; Well, clearly, they wanted

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:30.654
the utmost absolute charges.

00:00:30.787 --> 00:00:32.256
And I think with what we see

00:00:32.389 --> 00:00:33.624
today, they're going get that.

00:00:33.757 --> 00:00:34.491
John, I don't know the last

00:00:34.625 --> 00:00:37.494
time, if ever, I've seen a

00:00:37.561 --> 00:00:38.695
uniformed police officer under

00:00:38.829 --> 00:00:40.831
the color of law being charged

00:00:40.964 --> 00:00:41.632
with kidnapping.

00:00:41.765 --> 00:00:44.134
We have to take that in and

00:00:44.268 --> 00:00:46.069
really soak that for a moment

00:00:46.203 --> 00:00:48.038
and understand the gravity of

00:00:48.171 --> 00:00:50.974
what happened here to tyre.

00:00:51.108 --> 00:00:52.943
&gt;&gt; Why does that have particular

00:00:53.076 --> 00:00:54.478
gravity to you, the kidnapping

00:00:54.611 --> 00:00:54.945
charge?

00:00:54.945 --> 00:00:56.613
&gt;&gt; Well, you know, look, I've

00:00:56.747 --> 00:00:57.881
been thinking of all different

00:00:58.015 --> 00:00:59.016
ways to describe what happened

00:00:59.149 --> 00:01:00.717
on that video since it hasn't

00:01:00.851 --> 00:01:01.885
been released yet.

00:01:02.019 --> 00:01:03.520
And here is another way for me

00:01:03.553 --> 00:01:06.089
to describe it, which may give

00:01:06.223 --> 00:01:07.124
you some context.

00:01:07.524 --> 00:01:09.693
It was an mma fight, except

00:01:09.826 --> 00:01:12.329
there was only one side that was

00:01:12.462 --> 00:01:13.964
mma.
You know, tyre was helpless.

00:01:14.097 --> 00:01:15.032
He was defenseless.

00:01:15.165 --> 00:01:16.566
He was restrained.

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:17.901
And that's why you're seeing the

00:01:18.035 --> 00:01:19.803
types of charges that you're

00:01:19.936 --> 00:01:21.805
seeing here from second-degree

00:01:21.938 --> 00:01:24.107
murder to obstruction to

00:01:24.241 --> 00:01:25.142
aggravated assault to

00:01:25.542 --> 00:01:26.977
kidnapping, because he was

00:01:27.110 --> 00:01:29.913
literally, his freedom was taken

00:01:30.047 --> 00:01:32.215
away from him because he didn't

00:01:32.349 --> 00:01:33.550
do anything wrong.

00:01:33.550 --> 00:01:35.552
The proportionality of what

00:01:35.686 --> 00:01:40.190
happened here was so askew that

00:01:40.324 --> 00:01:41.558
it only warranted the highest

00:01:41.558 --> 00:01:42.225
level of charges.

00:01:42.359 --> 00:01:44.261
&gt;&gt; You just said it was like a

00:01:44.394 --> 00:01:45.762
one-sided mma fight.

00:01:45.896 --> 00:01:47.564
You also describe it as Mr.

00:01:47.564 --> 00:01:48.999
Nichols being treated like a

00:01:49.132 --> 00:01:50.267
human pinata.

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:51.201
Those were your words.

00:01:51.568 --> 00:01:52.869
Do you think Memphis, the

00:01:53.003 --> 00:01:54.504
community there, is prepared to

00:01:54.638 --> 00:01:56.106
see this video, which you have

00:01:56.239 --> 00:01:56.640
seen?

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:59.576
&gt;&gt; They're going to have to be

00:01:59.676 --> 00:02:00.143
prepared, John.

00:02:00.143 --> 00:02:01.044
I think one way to prepare them

00:02:01.178 --> 00:02:03.013
is for us to be able to describe

00:02:03.146 --> 00:02:04.981
it so hopefully when they do see

00:02:05.115 --> 00:02:06.316
it, especially along with the

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:08.418
charges, that there is peace.

00:02:08.552 --> 00:02:10.420
That is the goal.

00:02:10.554 --> 00:02:11.588
Should their voices be heard?

00:02:11.688 --> 00:02:12.089
Absolutely.

00:02:12.089 --> 00:02:14.691
There is no doubt about that.

00:02:14.825 --> 00:02:16.193
But there should be anything but

00:02:16.326 --> 00:02:17.694
peace in the streets?

00:02:17.828 --> 00:02:18.161
Correct.

00:02:18.161 --> 00:02:19.162
That's what we're looking for.

00:02:19.596 --> 00:02:20.964
&gt;&gt; What do you know about the

00:02:21.098 --> 00:02:23.033
traffic stop that took place

00:02:23.166 --> 00:02:24.267
that led up to this?

00:02:24.401 --> 00:02:24.935
Do you even know why he was

00:02:25.068 --> 00:02:27.270
stopped?

00:02:27.604 --> 00:02:28.739
&gt;&gt; No, we really don't.

00:02:28.872 --> 00:02:30.006
And that's not anything that I'm

00:02:30.140 --> 00:02:31.608
saying that's been withheld from

00:02:31.608 --> 00:02:34.511
us.
But we don't know yet.

00:02:34.644 --> 00:02:35.278
We know that the police have

00:02:35.612 --> 00:02:36.546
said that this was a traffic

00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:39.249
stop.
But we don't know more than

00:02:39.616 --> 00:02:40.817
that.
And quite frankly, I have to

00:02:40.951 --> 00:02:43.820
tell you, right now, I don't

00:02:43.954 --> 00:02:44.621
know that it's a justification

00:02:44.755 --> 00:02:45.889
that they're saying it was

00:02:46.022 --> 00:02:47.891
traffic stop.

00:02:48.024 --> 00:02:48.525
Because we know that the

00:02:48.658 --> 00:02:50.961
saturation and suppression units

00:02:51.094 --> 00:02:52.429
do use a pretext to stop in

00:02:52.562 --> 00:02:56.299
order to carry out this wolf

00:02:56.433 --> 00:02:58.468
gang-like mentality, this

00:02:58.602 --> 00:02:59.669
wolfpack mentality of policing.

00:02:59.803 --> 00:03:01.638
&gt;&gt; You have no specific

00:03:01.638 --> 00:03:02.272
knowledge that that's what

00:03:02.406 --> 00:03:03.039
happened here.

00:03:03.173 --> 00:03:06.710
You're suggesting, though, it's

00:03:06.843 --> 00:03:08.111
a possibility?

00:03:08.245 --> 00:03:09.646
&gt;&gt; It's only a possibility,

00:03:09.646 --> 00:03:10.146
that's correct.

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:11.915
&gt;&gt; I understand the preliminary

00:03:12.048 --> 00:03:12.783
results of an autopsy

00:03:12.916 --> 00:03:14.084
commissioned by you and attorney

00:03:14.217 --> 00:03:16.153
Ben crump and the family, those

00:03:16.286 --> 00:03:16.853
results are in.

00:03:16.987 --> 00:03:18.388
What do you know at this point

00:03:18.522 --> 00:03:19.222
about those results?

00:03:19.656 --> 00:03:20.857
&gt;&gt; So here's what I can tell you

00:03:20.991 --> 00:03:21.792
about those results.

00:03:21.925 --> 00:03:23.994
The results indicate that what

00:03:24.127 --> 00:03:27.664
we saw in the video are

00:03:27.664 --> 00:03:29.666
consistent with the a severe

00:03:29.666 --> 00:03:30.166
beating.

00:03:30.233 --> 00:03:33.003
And our independent medical

00:03:33.136 --> 00:03:34.237
examiner has authorized us to

00:03:34.371 --> 00:03:35.205
quote that.

00:03:35.338 --> 00:03:36.673
The injuries are consistent with

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:38.508
a severe beating.

00:03:38.642 --> 00:03:40.277
Meaning that the hemorrhage that

00:03:40.410 --> 00:03:42.145
was found was so deep that it

00:03:42.279 --> 00:03:45.682
could only be caused by blunt

00:03:45.682 --> 00:03:46.917
force trauma, which again is

00:03:47.050 --> 00:03:48.485
consistent with a severe

00:03:48.618 --> 00:03:48.952
beating.

00:03:48.952 --> 00:03:50.520
&gt;&gt; I know you've got a lot on

00:03:50.654 --> 00:03:52.088
your plate, as does the family.

00:03:52.222 --> 00:03:54.124
But lastly, does the family at

00:03:54.257 --> 00:03:55.692
this point intend to sue the

00:03:55.692 --> 00:03:57.694
city of Memphis?

00:03:57.794 --> 00:04:00.163
&gt;&gt; Well, I think a lawsuit is

00:04:00.297 --> 00:04:01.097
clearly on the horizon.

00:04:01.231 --> 00:04:02.666
I'm not going to tell you when

00:04:02.799 --> 00:04:03.800
that's going happen.

00:04:03.934 --> 00:04:06.136
We have to complete our

00:04:06.269 --> 00:04:06.703
investigation.

00:04:06.703 --> 00:04:07.704
And I'm hoping that the

00:04:07.704 --> 00:04:09.039
productive meeting that we had

00:04:09.172 --> 00:04:11.908
with the FBI, the doj, and the

00:04:12.042 --> 00:04:14.144
Shelby county state's attorney,

00:04:14.277 --> 00:04:15.712
that we've all committed to

00:04:15.779 --> 00:04:16.646
ourselves that we're going to

00:04:16.780 --> 00:04:17.714
cooperate with each other that

00:04:17.848 --> 00:04:18.648
that continues.

